{"title":"Career Roadmap — Ceramic Designer","role":"Ceramic Designer","summary":"A Ceramic Designer creates functional, decorative, architectural, artistic, or commercial objects using clay and ceramic materials.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Toy & Game Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Ceramic Designer creates functional, decorative, architectural, artistic, or commercial objects using clay and ceramic materials."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design"},{"text":"Material science"},{"text":"Craft"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Surface development"},{"text":"3D form development"},{"text":"Kiln and firing knowledge"},{"text":"Product thinking"},{"text":"Visual aesthetics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Ceramic Designers may work in tableware, home décor, sanitaryware, tiles, lifestyle products, art ceramics, architectural ceramics, studio pottery, luxury products and industrial ceramic applications."},{"type":"p","text":"A professional Ceramic Designer must understand not only how an object looks, but also how clay behaves, how it is manufactured, glazed, fired and finished."}]},{"heading":"What a Ceramic Designer Does","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developing ceramic product concepts"},{"text":"Sketching and visualising forms"},{"text":"Selecting appropriate clay bodies"},{"text":"Creating physical prototypes"},{"text":"Making moulds"},{"text":"Developing surface patterns"},{"text":"Selecting glazes"},{"text":"Testing firing conditions"},{"text":"Creating functional prototypes"},{"text":"Working with ceramic manufacturers"},{"text":"Preparing technical drawings"},{"text":"Conducting material experiments"},{"text":"Checking dimensional accuracy"},{"text":"Improving manufacturing efficiency"},{"text":"Developing collections and product ranges"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the industry, the designer may work primarily in a studio/craft environment, design studio, manufacturing facility, or product-development team."}]},{"heading":"Ceramic Designer vs Related Roles","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Role","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Ceramic Designer"},{"text":"Product/form/surface design using ceramics"}],[{"text":"Potter"},{"text":"Making ceramic objects, often through studio or craft practice"}],[{"text":"Ceramic Artist"},{"text":"Artistic and expressive ceramic work"}],[{"text":"Industrial Designer"},{"text":"Broader product design across materials"}],[{"text":"Ceramic Technologist"},{"text":"Technical/material/manufacturing performance"}],[{"text":"Tile Designer"},{"text":"Ceramic tile collections and surfaces"}],[{"text":"Product Designer"},{"text":"Commercial product development"}],[{"text":"Glass Designer"},{"text":"Objects and products using glass"}],[{"text":"Ceramic Engineer"},{"text":"Technical engineering applications of ceramics"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"A Ceramic Designer sits between creative design and material-based production."}]},{"heading":"Core Knowledge Required","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Material Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clay types"},{"text":"Earthenware"},{"text":"Stoneware"},{"text":"Porcelain"},{"text":"Ceramic additives"},{"text":"Plasticity"},{"text":"Shrinkage"},{"text":"Moisture"},{"text":"Drying"},{"text":"Firing"},{"text":"Thermal behaviour"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Form Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Proportion"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Symmetry"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Volume"},{"text":"Negative space"},{"text":"Structural stability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Surface Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Glazing"},{"text":"Textures"},{"text":"Patterns"},{"text":"Engraving"},{"text":"Inlay"},{"text":"Slip decoration"},{"text":"Underglaze"},{"text":"Overglaze"},{"text":"Digital surface graphics"}]}]},{"heading":"Ceramic Production Process","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A student should understand the complete workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research","Concept","Sketching","Form Development","Clay Selection","Prototype","Drying","Bisque Firing","Glazing / Surface Treatment","Glaze Firing","Quality Inspection","Final Product"]},{"type":"p","text":"This manufacturing understanding is essential because ceramics change considerably during drying and firing."}]},{"heading":"Ceramic Forming Techniques","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students should gain practical experience with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Hand Building"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pinch"},{"text":"Coil"},{"text":"Slab"},{"text":"Sculptural construction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Wheel Throwing"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cups"},{"text":"Bowls"},{"text":"Plates"},{"text":"Vessels"},{"text":"Cylindrical forms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Slip Casting"},{"type":"p","text":"Important for commercial production."},{"type":"p","text":"Process:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Master Model","Mould","Liquid Slip","Casting","Demoulding","Finishing"]},{"type":"h","text":"Pressing"},{"type":"p","text":"Used in industrial ceramic manufacturing."},{"type":"h","text":"Extrusion"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tiles"},{"text":"Profiles"},{"text":"Repeated forms"},{"text":"Architectural components"}]}]},{"heading":"Mould Making","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Mould development is an important professional skill."},{"type":"p","text":"Students should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Plaster moulds"},{"text":"Multi-part moulds"},{"text":"Master models"},{"text":"Draft angles"},{"text":"Parting lines"},{"text":"Release requirements"},{"text":"Repetition and production efficiency"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For commercial products, the ability to convert a prototype into a repeatable manufacturing process is extremely valuable."}]},{"heading":"Glaze & Surface Development","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Glazing requires both artistic and technical understanding."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Glaze composition basics"},{"text":"Colourants"},{"text":"Application techniques"},{"text":"Glaze thickness"},{"text":"Surface defects"},{"text":"Firing temperature"},{"text":"Glaze compatibility"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Common defects include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Crawling"},{"text":"Crazing"},{"text":"Pinholing"},{"text":"Blistering"},{"text":"Running"},{"text":"Uneven coverage"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Students should maintain a glaze test library documenting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Recipe/reference"},{"text":"Application method"},{"text":"Firing conditions"},{"text":"Result"},{"text":"Defects"},{"text":"Possible modifications"}]}]},{"heading":"Design Software","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Digital skills increasingly complement traditional ceramic skills."},{"type":"h","text":"2D"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Adobe Illustrator"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Figma"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3D"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"Fusion 360"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"SolidWorks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rendering"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"KeyShot"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"Other rendering workflows"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Fabrication"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the basics of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"CNC"},{"text":"Laser cutting"},{"text":"Digital mould-making"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact software depends on the employer and production environment."}]},{"heading":"3D Printing & Digital Ceramics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Digital fabrication is creating new possibilities for ceramic design."},{"type":"p","text":"Students can explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ceramic 3D printing"},{"text":"Printed moulds"},{"text":"Parametric forms"},{"text":"Computational patterns"},{"text":"CNC mould-making"},{"text":"Digital slip-casting systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential workflow:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Digital Model","CAD / 3D Design","Digital Prototype","3D Printed Master / Mould","Ceramic Production","Firing","Final Object"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is a strong intersection between traditional craft and digital manufacturing."}]},{"heading":"B.Des Academic Roadmap","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Design & Material Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design fundamentals"},{"text":"Drawing"},{"text":"Form studies"},{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Basic material exploration"},{"text":"Design thinking"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Begin practical ceramic work:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clay preparation"},{"text":"Hand building"},{"text":"Basic firing"},{"text":"Surface experimentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a material-experiment portfolio."}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Ceramic Design Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wheel throwing"},{"text":"Slip casting"},{"text":"Mould making"},{"text":"Glazing"},{"text":"Kiln operation"},{"text":"Ceramic surface design"},{"text":"Product ergonomics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Begin digital design:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rhino/Blender"},{"text":"Illustrator"},{"text":"Basic rendering"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Projects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tableware collection"},{"text":"Decorative vessel series"},{"text":"Ceramic lighting concept"},{"text":"Tile pattern collection"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Product & Industrial Ceramic Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Commercial ceramics"},{"text":"Production processes"},{"text":"Manufacturing constraints"},{"text":"Material optimisation"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Sustainable materials"},{"text":"Cost awareness"},{"text":"Packaging"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Explore industry sectors such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tableware"},{"text":"Tiles"},{"text":"Sanitaryware"},{"text":"Home décor"},{"text":"Architectural ceramics"},{"text":"Lifestyle products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target"},{"type":"p","text":"Complete at least one project from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Concept","Prototype","Manufacturing","Final Product"]}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Professional Ceramic Collection","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The final-year project should demonstrate a complete design system rather than one isolated object."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible projects:"},{"type":"h","text":"Sustainable Tableware"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a low-waste ceramic tableware collection."},{"type":"h","text":"Contemporary Indian Ceramics"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine traditional craft knowledge with contemporary product design."},{"type":"h","text":"Modular Tiles"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop a modular architectural surface system."},{"type":"h","text":"Ceramic Lighting"},{"type":"p","text":"Design ceramic shades or lighting components."},{"type":"h","text":"Smart Kitchenware"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore functional ceramic products integrated with modern living."},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Ceramics"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a digitally fabricated ceramic collection."}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Structure","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong Ceramic Designer portfolio should demonstrate material experimentation + design thinking + manufacturing understanding."},{"type":"p","text":"For each project:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research","Inspiration","Material Experiments","Concept Development","Sketches","Form Exploration","Prototype","Technical Development","Firing / Testing","Iteration","Final Product"]},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sketches"},{"text":"Material tests"},{"text":"Clay samples"},{"text":"Glaze experiments"},{"text":"Form studies"},{"text":"Mould development"},{"text":"CAD models"},{"text":"Technical drawings"},{"text":"Process photographs"},{"text":"Final product photography"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Portfolio Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Project","Skills Demonstrated"],"rows":[[{"text":"Tableware Collection"},{"text":"Functional design"}],[{"text":"Ceramic Lighting"},{"text":"Form + function"}],[{"text":"Tile Collection"},{"text":"Pattern + production"}],[{"text":"Ceramic Home Décor"},{"text":"Commercial design"}],[{"text":"Sustainable Ceramics"},{"text":"Material innovation"}],[{"text":"Architectural Ceramics"},{"text":"Scale + systems"}],[{"text":"Experimental Glaze Series"},{"text":"Material research"}],[{"text":"Ceramic Jewellery"},{"text":"Small-scale precision"}],[{"text":"Digital Ceramic Collection"},{"text":"CAD + fabrication"}],[{"text":"Traditional Craft Reinterpretation"},{"text":"Cultural design"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"A portfolio should contain both experimental work and commercially relevant projects."}]},{"heading":"Ergonomics & Functional Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For functional ceramic products, students need to understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Grip"},{"text":"Weight"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Handle dimensions"},{"text":"Pouring"},{"text":"Drinking"},{"text":"Cleaning"},{"text":"Heat exposure"},{"text":"Stability"},{"text":"Stackability"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For example, designing a cup is not simply:"},{"type":"p","text":"“Make an attractive shape.”"},{"type":"p","text":"The designer must consider:"},{"type":"p","text":"How does the user hold it, drink from it, clean it, store it and manufacture it?"}]},{"heading":"Industrial Production Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students targeting commercial roles should understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mass production"},{"text":"Batch production"},{"text":"Tolerances"},{"text":"Mould design"},{"text":"Production cycles"},{"text":"Material costs"},{"text":"Labour"},{"text":"Packaging"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Defect rates"},{"text":"Supply chains"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Common production methods may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Slip casting"},{"text":"Pressing"},{"text":"Jiggering/jolleying"},{"text":"Extrusion"},{"text":"Industrial glazing"},{"text":"Automated finishing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact process depends on the product category."}]},{"heading":"Sustainability","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Ceramic production can have significant energy and material implications."},{"type":"p","text":"Students should study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Energy-efficient firing"},{"text":"Kiln efficiency"},{"text":"Waste reduction"},{"text":"Material recycling"},{"text":"Water management"},{"text":"Glaze safety"},{"text":"Local materials"},{"text":"Durable product design"},{"text":"Repairability"},{"text":"Long product life"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sustainable design principle"},{"type":"p","text":"Design for durability rather than disposability."},{"type":"p","text":"Ceramics can have a long usable life, making durability and responsible production important sustainability considerations."}]},{"heading":"Traditional Indian Ceramic & Craft Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For students in India, knowledge of traditional ceramic and craft practices can be valuable."},{"type":"p","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Terracotta"},{"text":"Studio pottery"},{"text":"Regional pottery traditions"},{"text":"Traditional kiln techniques"},{"text":"Indigenous surface treatments"},{"text":"Craft communities"},{"text":"Contemporary craft entrepreneurship"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, traditional techniques should be studied respectfully, with attention to craft attribution, community knowledge and fair collaboration."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Suitable internships include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ceramic Design Intern"},{"text":"Product Design Intern"},{"text":"Tableware Design Intern"},{"text":"Tile Design Intern"},{"text":"Surface Design Intern"},{"text":"Ceramic Production Intern"},{"text":"Craft Design Intern"},{"text":"Home Décor Design Intern"},{"text":"Industrial Design Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Suitable environments"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ceramic studios"},{"text":"Tableware manufacturers"},{"text":"Tile companies"},{"text":"Sanitaryware manufacturers"},{"text":"Home décor brands"},{"text":"Craft clusters"},{"text":"Design studios"},{"text":"Architectural material companies"},{"text":"Lifestyle brands"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A production-oriented internship is particularly valuable because students learn how designs move from prototype to manufacturable product."}]},{"heading":"Career Specialisations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"1. Tableware Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Design:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Plates"},{"text":"Cups"},{"text":"Bowls"},{"text":"Serving ware"},{"text":"Kitchen products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Tile Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patterns"},{"text":"Surfaces"},{"text":"Modular systems"},{"text":"Architectural applications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Ceramic Product Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Design:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Home products"},{"text":"Décor"},{"text":"Lifestyle objects"}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Ceramic Artist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sculptural"},{"text":"Experimental"},{"text":"Gallery-oriented work"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Ceramic Surface Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Glaze"},{"text":"Texture"},{"text":"Pattern"},{"text":"Decoration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Architectural Ceramic Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Facades"},{"text":"Tiles"},{"text":"Wall systems"},{"text":"Architectural installations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"7. Ceramic CAD Designer"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital modelling"},{"text":"Production-ready geometry"},{"text":"Mould development"}]}]},{"heading":"Glass Design Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Although the target career is Ceramic Designer, the B.Des specialisation also includes Ceramic & Glass Design."},{"type":"p","text":"Students can therefore develop complementary knowledge in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Glass forming"},{"text":"Blown glass"},{"text":"Kiln forming"},{"text":"Fusing"},{"text":"Slumping"},{"text":"Glass casting"},{"text":"Glass surface treatment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This can create additional opportunities in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Tableware"},{"text":"Decorative products"},{"text":"Architectural applications"},{"text":"Lifestyle products"}]}]},{"heading":"AI & Ceramic Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI can support ceramic designers in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Concept exploration"},{"text":"Pattern generation"},{"text":"Collection development"},{"text":"Moodboards"},{"text":"Form ideation"},{"text":"Surface pattern exploration"},{"text":"Market trend analysis"},{"text":"Product visualisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A practical workflow could be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Design Brief","AI-assisted Concept Exploration","Human Selection","Sketch","CAD Model","Physical Prototype","Material Testing","Final Product"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI-generated concepts still need to be validated against:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Manufacturing feasibility"},{"text":"Material behaviour"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Structural stability"},{"text":"Cost"},{"text":"Sustainability"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant postgraduate pathways include:"},{"type":"h","text":"M.Des"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible specialisations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ceramic Design"},{"text":"Product Design"},{"text":"Industrial Design"},{"text":"Craft Design"},{"text":"Sustainable Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Master's"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Ceramics"},{"text":"MFA Ceramics"},{"text":"Material Design"},{"text":"Product Design"},{"text":"Surface Design"},{"text":"Craft Design"},{"text":"Design Management"},{"text":"Sustainable Design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"An MFA may be more appropriate for students pursuing studio art or artistic practice, while an M.Des may be better suited to product and commercial design."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Typical industry pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Ceramic Design Intern","Junior Ceramic Designer","Ceramic Designer","Senior Ceramic Designer","Lead Designer","Design Manager","Design Director"]},{"type":"p","text":"Alternative entrepreneurial pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Studio Assistant","Independent Ceramic Practice","Small Ceramic Brand","Design Studio / Workshop","Brand Founder"]}]},{"heading":"Related Careers","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A graduate can also move into:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ceramic Designer"},{"text":"Product Designer"},{"text":"Tableware Designer"},{"text":"Tile Designer"},{"text":"Surface Designer"},{"text":"Home Décor Designer"},{"text":"Industrial Designer"},{"text":"Craft Designer"},{"text":"Ceramic Artist"},{"text":"Material Designer"},{"text":"CAD Designer"},{"text":"Architectural Material Designer"},{"text":"Glass Designer"},{"text":"Design Researcher"},{"text":"Design Entrepreneur"}]}]},{"heading":"Skill-Gap Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Beginner","Job Ready","Advanced"],"rows":[[{"text":"Clay Handling"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Expert"}],[{"text":"Wheel Throwing"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Intermediate"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Mould Making"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Glazing"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Expert"}],[{"text":"Kiln Knowledge"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Product Design"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Intermediate"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Surface Design"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Sustainability"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Intermediate"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Portfolio Development"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"Strong"},{"text":"Advanced"}]]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product design"},{"text":"Form development"},{"text":"Sketching"},{"text":"Visualisation"},{"text":"Design research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ceramic"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clay preparation"},{"text":"Hand building"},{"text":"Wheel throwing"},{"text":"Slip casting"},{"text":"Mould making"},{"text":"Glazing"},{"text":"Kiln operation"},{"text":"Surface development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rhino / Blender"},{"text":"Illustrator"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"Digital rendering"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Manufacturing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Production processes"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Material testing"},{"text":"Technical drawings"},{"text":"Cost awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Client communication"},{"text":"Design documentation"},{"text":"Collaboration"},{"text":"Collection development"}]}]},{"heading":"Placement & Interview Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students should be able to explain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Why did you choose this clay body?"},{"text":"Why did you select this forming technique?"},{"text":"How did firing affect your design?"},{"text":"How did you solve shrinkage?"},{"text":"How did you develop the glaze?"},{"text":"How can this design be mass-produced?"},{"text":"How would you reduce manufacturing waste?"},{"text":"How did you test the ergonomics?"},{"text":"Why is your design commercially relevant?"},{"text":"How would you modify this design for a different customer segment?"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Employers may evaluate both creative quality and material/process understanding."}]},{"heading":"What Students Should Avoid","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"❌ Only creating decorative objects"},{"type":"p","text":"Commercial Ceramic Designers must understand function and production."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Ignoring manufacturing"},{"type":"p","text":"A beautiful prototype that cannot be produced efficiently has limited commercial value."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Depending entirely on handcraft"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital modelling and manufacturing knowledge can significantly broaden career options."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Ignoring glaze/material testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Ceramic outcomes are highly dependent on materials and firing."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Building a portfolio only from final photographs"},{"type":"p","text":"The design process is extremely important."},{"type":"h","text":"❌ Collecting certificates instead of developing craft skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Hands-on material experience is more valuable for this career."}]},{"heading":"Ideal 4-Year Development Plan","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Focus","Expected Output"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Design + material fundamentals"},{"text":"Material experiments"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Ceramic techniques"},{"text":"4–6 ceramic projects"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Product + manufacturing"},{"text":"Commercial collection"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Specialisation + portfolio"},{"text":"4–6 polished case studies"}]]}]},{"heading":"Best Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, an ideal candidate should have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Des in Ceramic & Glass Design"},{"text":"Strong understanding of ceramic materials"},{"text":"Hand-building skills"},{"text":"Wheel-throwing experience"},{"text":"Slip-casting knowledge"},{"text":"Mould-making ability"},{"text":"Glazing and surface-development skills"},{"text":"Kiln and firing knowledge"},{"text":"Product-design fundamentals"},{"text":"Ergonomics knowledge"},{"text":"CAD/3D modelling skills"},{"text":"Basic digital fabrication knowledge"},{"text":"Manufacturing awareness"},{"text":"Sustainability knowledge"},{"text":"1–2 internships or equivalent studio/industry experience"},{"text":"4–6 strong portfolio collections"},{"text":"Physical prototypes"},{"text":"Professional product photography"},{"text":"CAD models and technical drawings"},{"text":"Material/glaze experiment documentation"},{"text":"At least one commercially oriented collection"},{"text":"At least one experimental or sustainable project"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strongest Graduate Profile"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Ceramic & Glass Design","Strong Ceramic Craft Skills","Glaze & Kiln Knowledge","CAD/3D Modelling","Product Design","Manufacturing Understanding","Sustainable Materials","Physical Prototypes","4–6 Portfolio Collections","Industry/Studio Experience"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This profile keeps the graduate open to careers in ceramic product design, tableware, tiles, home décor, architectural ceramics, surface design, material design, studio ceramics and design entrepreneurship."}]}]}